## Lore

The blind warrior women of Altara are among the best known of the Splugorth''s lesser minions, because four to six of them ride every Splugorth slave barge and help capture and herd the slaves. Each is an exceptional fighter with heightened senses and martial arts training. The Coalition has guessed they are juicers or crazies; others take them for D-bee psychics, which is nearer the truth.

The Splugorth conquered the Altarains some 2000 years ago and have bred them through generations of mind control, bio-wizard experimentation and brutality to accept slavery. They obey the Splugorth''s elite minions without hesitation, for anything else means death, and many have come to enjoy their place. But about a quarter hate their captivity and defy, fight or flee whenever they can. Runaways are hunted by Slavers, Conservators and their own sisters; the fiercest are killed on the spot and the rest returned for reconditioning, experimentation, the arena or hard labor.

There are no Altarain men. Born blind but otherwise healthy, the women are instinctive warriors and paladin-like crusaders with nearly indomitable wills and a hunger for challenge, adventure and combat. They are usually silent. Alignment: any, but typically anarchist or evil. Height 5.8 to 6.2 ft (1.7 to 1.9 m), weight about 160 lbs (72 kg), always very attractive. NPCs are typically 4th to 10th level (2D4+2).

## Equipment

Standard issue to warriors accompanying a Splugorth Slaver: a conventional dagger, vibro-blade, net gun, laser wrist blaster and mental incapacitator. They can use most other energy and hand-held weapons. Her only armor is a light, padded M.D.C. suit and helmet (30 M.D.C.); rogues may wear any armor but prefer light types for mobility.

Bio-wizard devices vary with the assignment; aerobes, aquarobes, clotrobes, purirobes, stasirobes and watrobes are common. Those who show great loyalty and bravery are occasionally awarded an Absurr life node symbiote or a chest amalgamate, either of which makes her an M.D.C. creature. Available upon assignment: Eylor floating eyes, Eylor seeker-hunter, forearm plasma blaster, helmet laser, jolt gun, microbes, plasma rifle, psi-interrogator, a telepathic holographic imager (special operatives and officers), and symbiotic organisms (limited; dangerous parasites are never used on loyal minions).
